t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>In a White House press briefing today, President Donald J. Trump took questions from reporters alongside Vice President JD Vance and Secretary of State Marco Rubio.</strong> Fresh off his return from Asia, President Trump used the briefing to underscore that America is negotiating from a position of restored strength — highlighting <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2026/11/president-trump-brings-home-billions-in-economic-growth-and-strengthens-americas-security/\">more than $17 billion</a> in deals that put American workers, farmers, and families first. He also made clear that he is ready to work across the aisle, especially on healthcare, to deliver results for the American people.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>On the historic Asia trip:</strong> “Last night, we returned home from one of the most successful presidential visits to Asia in American history&#8230; In four days, I met more than 20 world leaders, secured two new trade deals and about ten others coming very soon, attended four major international summits, reaffirmed America’s alliances throughout the region, and advanced the cause of peace and security around the world.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123832470822932512\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On working with Democrats:</strong> “Because of the power of the veto, there’s a real possibility that we’ll get a lot of great things done, especially on healthcare. I’m open to great healthcare. Now, can it be what they want? No, but it can be a combination of what we all want — and we could end up with great healthcare in our country.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123848950146826371\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On trade with Thailand:</strong> “Thailand signed an agreement to eliminate all tariffs on American products… and remove their non-tariff barriers, and they want to buy $2.6 billion a year in U.S. agricultural products, and we’re going to increase that number… Our farmers are a big beneficiary of this trip.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123837956054261930\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On trade with the Philippines:</strong> “Philippine Airlines will purchase… 20 brand new Boeing 787 Dreamliners with General Electric engines. It’s a big contract, supporting 47,000 American jobs.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123837519439773947\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On permitting reform:</strong> “Last night, landmark permitting reform legislation passed the Senate. It’s one of the biggest things that you will see. It’s a big deal&#8230; Now, it goes to the House — and if passed, it’s projected to put at least $1,300/year back in the pockets of hardworking Americans. But it’s even beyond that; it’s going to cause tremendous amounts of new building.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123834359153111161?s=20\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On the trilateral summit and nuclear security:</strong> “We discussed the responsibility of the world’s three largest nuclear powers… to reduce the risk that these weapons pose to the world… We spoke about the need to cooperate to stop the proliferation of that nuclear threat throughout our planet. And in particular, we talked extensively about ensuring that Iran will never have a nuclear weapon.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123840519067287987\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On meeting President Putin:</strong> “I held a bilateral meeting with President Putin of Russia, who clearly expressed his desire to see the war between Russia and Ukraine end by diplomatic means.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123838429884744163\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On economic strength:</strong> “The United States entered this trip from a position of unmatched economic and diplomatic strength… Already, gasoline is down 60 cents a gallon from just one month ago, and it’s going to be dropping fast.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123833100207620343\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On Iran:</strong> “They want to make a deal, but they don’t want to make a deal that’s acceptable to me. We want to make a real deal, not a fake deal that they’ve been doing for 51 years… They’ve been bullshitting people for 51 years.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123833098551038180\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On American strength:</strong> “Everywhere I went on this trip and every leader I met, it was clear that America is respected again like never before. We are respected.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123835436397478267\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On keeping critical infrastructure in America:</strong> “Whoever wins SI wins… We’re not going to allow our companies to build data centers outside of our country. We’re not going to allow that to happen. You know, they allowed that to happen with chips and everything else and it was very destructive to our country… We want them to build it here.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123836545346285698\">Watch</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/at-press-briefing-president-trump-touts-historic-wins-for-americans-signals-deal-making-on-healthcare/\">At Press Briefing, President Trump Touts Historic Wins for Americans, Signals Deal-Making on Healthcare</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
